From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:46:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vkr, vrend: survive an unexportable guest resource, and say why

With SurfaceFlinger and HWUI both on Venus in the AAOS guest,
system_server dies every few minutes:

    proxy: exported res 2641 to unexpected fd_type -1
    vkr: failed to query resource props: invalid res_id 2641
    vkr: vkGetMemoryResourcePropertiesMESA resulted in CS error
    vkr: destroying context 18 (android framework) with a valid instance

and in the guest, GrallocUploadThread aborts in vn_relax <-
vn_ring_submit_command <- vn_get_memory_dma_buf_properties <-
vn_GetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR while TaskSnapshotPersister uploads a
hardware bitmap. The proxy only attaches a guest resource to a
render-server context when it exports as a dma-buf; a resource vrend
backed with a plain GL texture never gets there, and the guest's
properties query for it is treated as a fatal stream error. It is not:
the stream is fine, the buffer is merely not importable. Return
VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE exactly as the exists-but-not-dma-buf
branch already does, so HWUI falls back instead of the process dying.

Separately, log why vrend_resource_gbm_init() declined to give a
resource GBM backing (format without a GBM equivalent, mipmaps/3D/MSAA,
no GBM device or usable format/flags, bind flags without SCANOUT|SHARED,
GBM layout feature not negotiated, gbm_device_is_format_supported()
saying no, or gbm_bo_create() failing), with the resource's size, format
and bind flags, so the next "unexpected fd_type -1" can be traced to its
cause rather than guessed. It goes through virgl_debug(), so it prints
only with VIRGL_LOG_LEVEL=debug (the message is formatted either way).

This is the virglrenderer 1.3.0 version. In 1.3.0
vrend_resource_gbm_init() gained another early return: a non-MINIGBM
build gives a resource no GBM backing unless the GBM layout feature was
negotiated (vrend_state.gbm_layout_feat, which needs
VIRGL_GBM_LAYOUT_ENABLE or VIRGL_GBM_LAYOUT_FORCE_ENABLE). The
diagnostic hunk follows the 1.3.0 function and names that reason too.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c    | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
index ffe621bc..d97b5c09 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -433,8 +433,22 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkGetMemoryResourcePropertiesMESA(
 
    struct vkr_resource *res = vkr_context_get_resource(ctx, args->resourceId);
    if (!res) {
-      vkr_log("failed to query resource props: invalid res_id %u", args->resourceId);
-      vkr_context_set_fatal(ctx);
+      /*
+       * Not a stream error. With the render server, the proxy attaches a
+       * guest resource to this context only if it exports as a dma-buf
+       * (proxy_context.c: "exported res %d to unexpected fd_type"). A
+       * gralloc buffer the host backed with a plain GL texture therefore
+       * never reaches us, and the guest's next vkGetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR on
+       * it lands here. Killing the context for that aborts the guest process
+       * in vn_relax -- measured on RPi4: system_server's GrallocUploadThread
+       * dies importing a TaskSnapshot bitmap, and zygote restarts. Answer the
+       * way the exists-but-not-a-dma-buf case below already does, so the
+       * caller (HWUI) can fall back.
+       */
+      vkr_log("failed to query resource props: res_id %u not attached to this "
+              "context (not exportable as a dma-buf?), answering "
+              "VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE", args->resourceId);
+      args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
       return;
    }
 
diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 4bf88e09..4f057dd6 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -8590,19 +8590,32 @@ static void vrend_resource_gbm_init(struct vrend_resource *gr, uint32_t format)
 #if defined(HAVE_EPOXY_EGL_H) && defined(ENABLE_GBM_ALLOCATION)
    uint32_t gbm_flags = virgl_gbm_convert_flags(gr->base.bind);
    uint32_t gbm_format = 0;
+   /*
+    * Every early-out below leaves the resource as a plain GL texture, which
+    * cannot be exported as a dma-buf and therefore cannot be imported by a
+    * Venus (guest Vulkan) client. Name the reason, once per resource, so an
+    * "unexpected fd_type -1" in the proxy log can be traced to it.
+    */
+#define GBM_INIT_SKIP(why) \
+   do { \
+      virgl_debug("%s: res %ux%u virgl_format %u bind 0x%x: no GBM backing: %s\n", \
+                  __func__, gr->base.width0, gr->base.height0, format, \
+                  gr->base.bind, why); \
+      return; \
+   } while (0)
    if (virgl_gbm_convert_format(&format, &gbm_format))
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("format has no GBM equivalent");
    if (vrend_winsys_different_gpu())
       gbm_flags |= GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR;
 
    if (gr->base.depth0 != 1 || gr->base.last_level != 0 || gr->base.nr_samples > 1)
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("3D, mipmapped or multisampled");
 
    if (!gbm || !gbm->device || !gbm_format || !gbm_flags)
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("no gbm device, or no usable format/flags");
 
    if (!virgl_gbm_external_allocation_preferred(gr->base.bind))
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("bind flags have neither SCANOUT nor SHARED");
 
 #if !defined(MINIGBM)
    /*
@@ -8610,7 +8623,7 @@ static void vrend_resource_gbm_init(struct vrend_resource *gr, uint32_t format)
     * Skip GBM allocation when we don't actually need it.
     */
    if (!vrend_state.gbm_layout_feat)
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("GBM layout feature not negotiated (1.3.0 skips GBM then)");
 
    /*
     * Kernel virtio-gpu driver doesn't support modifiers other than linear and
@@ -8623,12 +8636,13 @@ static void vrend_resource_gbm_init(struct vrend_resource *gr, uint32_t format)
 #endif
 
    if (!gbm_device_is_format_supported(gbm->device, gbm_format, gbm_flags))
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("gbm_device_is_format_supported() says no for this format/usage");
 
    struct gbm_bo *bo = gbm_bo_create(gbm->device, gr->base.width0, gr->base.height0,
                                      gbm_format, gbm_flags);
    if (!bo)
-      return;
+      GBM_INIT_SKIP("gbm_bo_create() failed");
+#undef GBM_INIT_SKIP
 
    gr->gbm_bo = bo;
    gr->storage_bits |= VREND_STORAGE_GBM_BUFFER;
